Mobile robots are utilized in a wide range of applications, including assisting humans \cite{robla2017working}, medical fields \cite{okamura2010medical, goher2017assessment}, and product transportation \cite{antony2018food}. When multiple robots operate in environments with human employees, collisions between robots and humans can occur \cite{robla2017working, han2021analysis}. Numerous sensors and indoor sensing methods have been deployed on robots, which are crucial for applications such as robotic navigation in large industrial factories. However, detecting targets around blind corners remains a significant challenge.


