Furthermore, the median overall distance errors are 6.01\,cm at 2\,m, 7.47\,cm at 2.5\,m, 8.93\,cm at 3\,m, 11.19\,cm at 3.5\,m, and 11.81\,cm at 4\,m. These improvements can be attributed to our reconfigurable IRS design and the time slot allocation algorithm, which increases the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) by assigning more time slots to targets. As a result, \sn demonstrates strong potential for applications in robot-human interaction, particularly in factory environments where workers are not equipped with identifiers specifically designed for robotic systems.

