\section{Conclusion}

This paper presents \sn, a novel mmWave NLoS sensing system designed for precise, device-free indoor localization using a single radar and an  IRS. The system leverages a VAA-based reconfigurable IRS and integrates with existing FMCW signals. A key innovation of \sn is its antenna modulation scheme, which enables efficient radar-IRS communication, dynamic reflection angle adjustments, and effective differentiation of the IRS from static reflectors. By utilizing a frequency-based antenna encoding scheme and time slot allocation algorithm, the system effectively handles signal separation, improves SNR, and reduces sensing latency and support multiple radars and multiple targets scenarios.
Extensive evaluations in diverse indoor environments demonstrate that \sn achieves high accuracy in device-free localization, even under challenging NLoS conditions. These results highlight the system’s substantial potential for real-world applications, particularly in enabling safe and efficient robot-human interaction in complex indoor environments.




