\end{equation}
Thus, the elastic modulus, $E$, is strain-dependent, and is used for modelling the nonlinear behaviour in SPH. The strain-independent elastic modulus is obtained as $\epsilon^{xx} \rightarrow$ 0; the value $6.4$ GPa is obtained, which is also used in the SPH simulations later.


