The structural topology of the unit cell of a single monomer, as depicted in \autoref{fig_1}, is first constructed and replicated in the $x$, $y$, and $z$ directions as required. The simulation box is subjected to periodic boundary conditions, implying that the polyimide chain has infinite length. The conjugate gradient method for energy minimization is performed following that. The timestep size is established at $0.1$ femtoseconds (fs), followed by equilibration in the NVT ensemble at a temperature of $500$K for a duration of $10^4$ femtoseconds. Subsequently, NPT ensemble equilibrations are conducted to incrementally adjust the temperature to 300K and the pressure to 1 atm.




The simulation box is stretched in the $x$ direction by an engineering strain rate of $0.000005$/fs to calculate the elastic modulus. The box is remapped accordingly, ensuring homogeneous deformation according to the Cauchy-Born rule. This is done in NVE ensemble for $10^5$ steps. These steps are termed production run, and throughout the production run, the virial stress, defined in \eqref{eq:four}, is calculated and monitored.

\begin{equation}
\sigma_v^{\alpha \beta} = -\frac{1}{V} \sum_i \left( (v_i^\alpha - \langle v_i \rangle^\alpha)(v_i^\beta - \langle v_i \rangle^\beta) \right) + \sum_{j > i} F_c^{\alpha, ij} x_{ij}^\beta
\label{eq:four}
\end{equation}

In Eq. \eqref{eq:four}, the $\sigma_v^{\alpha \beta}$ represents the virial stress tensor's $\alpha$ and $\beta$ component. $\langle v_i \rangle^\alpha$ denotes the component of average velocity vector in the neighbourhood of atom $i$ in the direction $\alpha$, and $v_i^\beta$ is the component of velocity vector of atom $i$ along $\beta$ direction. $F_c^{\alpha, ij}$ is the component of force exerted by atom $j$ on $i$ along $\alpha$ direction, while $x_{ij}^\beta$ is the difference between the $\beta^{th}$ component of the position vectors of $i$ and $j$.

