    Experimental results suggest that optimal performance often requires moderate $\alpha$ and larger $\lambda$. 
    Specifically, the former $\alpha$ ensures a balance between personalized and global prototypes during fusion, while the latter $\lambda$ ensures fusion occurs only among semantically similar local clients to prevent knowledge confusion.



