\subsection{Dealing with failures} \label{sec:framework:backtracking}
Till now, we worked with an assumption that $\B$ is large enough which gave us a successful evacuation.
The following algorithm is a rather standard binary search for the appropriate value of $\B$. 
%
Namely, if $\B$ is too small, then some agents cannot evacuate as a result of the execution of Algorithm \ref{alg:OneAttempt} with that particular $\B$ being part of the input.
%
Then, we use Lemma~\ref{lem:colored-zones} to ensure that non-evacuated agents are back at their homebases, we double $\B$ and start over (see Algorithm \ref{alg:Evacuation}).

\begin{figure}[htb]
