Let the set of exits in the constructed graph $G$ consist of the centers of all the stars, i.e., $X = \{ v_{0}^0, v_0^1, \ldots, v_0^k \}$.

Consider any spanning tree $T$ of $G$. First, suppose that $T$ contains all edges $\{ v_0^j, v_i^j\} $ of each star $S_n^j$ and consider the case with all nodes $v_i^0$ initially occupied by agents, i.e., $H = \{v_{1}^0, \ldots, v_{n}^0\}$.
