during the next $s$ steps, two agents per step can evacuate through exits $v_0^0$ and 
$v_0^1$ and so on. So, after $sk$ steps, at most $sk(k+1)/2$ agents can evacuate.
Clearly, this bound is reachable. 
Now consider the strategy which uses only the tree $T$.
