In this work, instead of scheduling such complex traffic on-the-fly and augmenting isolation support on each system component, we propose to model traffic as network flows and proactively re-shape the traffic to avoid unpredictable contention. 
We discuss the implications of our findings on the design of future I/O management stacks and device interfaces.



