First, existing traffic management solutions for I/O accelerators suffer from breakage of isolation. 
For example, naively rate limiting input data streams at X Gbps~\cite{grant2020fairnic} or treating accelerator messages as packets during fair queuing~\cite{liu2019ipipe,eran2019nica} fail to allocate accelerator throughput to be X Gbps. %do not take the heterogeneity and non-linearity into account.  
