It's now time to introduce extended word equations. We start with some motivation before giving a formal definition. Consider the word equation $(\mathit{XXY}, \mathit{ZWZ})$. We want a representation of this word equation that encodes partial information about the relative lengths of the variables. One natural way to do this would be with a diagram like the one in Figure~\ref{fig-xxy-zwz}.

