$$\mathcal{E} = \{b_1=0, e_1=b_2, e_2=b_3, \ldots, e_{J-1}=b_J, e_J=T\}.$$

For each interval $I_{j} = [b_{j}, e_{j}[$:
\begin{itemize}
\item We compute the intersection of the execution of each task %of all processors 
with~$I_{j}$. 
Since the schedule~$\sigma$ is given, we can complete this step in linear time. 
We let $\mathcal{Q}^{j}$ be the subset of tasks intersecting with~$I_{j}$, i.e., 
$$u\in \mathcal{Q}^{j} \quad \Leftrightarrow \quad [\sigma(u), \sigma(u)+ \omega(u) [ \;\;  \cap  \;\; I_j \neq \emptyset . $$
