\begin{proof}[Proof of Remark \ref{remark:lower_bound_abf}]
In $\assignranks_{\rho}$, the $n$ agents are eventually splited to $\rho$ \emph{deputies} and $n-\rho > n/2$ \emph{recipients}. 
Before assigning the $n$ agents unique ranks, each recipient must meet at least one deputy,
which requires at least $\sum_{i=1}^{n-\rho} \binom{n}{2}/(2i \rho)=\Theta(\sfrac{n^2}{r}\cdot \log n)$ expected interactions, i.e., $\Theta(\sfrac{n}{r}\cdot \log n)$ time.
