\textit{2) \textbf{Access Services:}} In LAE networks, LAVs may perform tasks in remote areas, such as collecting environmental data. 
However, complex terrain makes it difficult for terrestrial networks to provide access services to LAVs operating in these areas.
% It is challenging for terrestrial networks to provide access services to LAVs in these areas, as the complex terrain hinders the deployment of network infrastructures. 
Accessing satellite networks is an efficient solution for connecting remote users \cite{he2024toward}.
% To ensure the LAVs remain connected, satellites can be utilized to provide access services to LAVs, connecting them to their control centers. 
