\textbf{Orthogonal planar reduction.}
The reduction hinges on the observation that substantial information from volumes can be preserved given their cross sections from multiple viewpoints (Figure \ref{fig:ortho}).
For instance, a feature specific to the left or right side of the brain may be lost from a sagittal profile, but can be recovered when also given the axial profile.

