\textbf{Evaluation method.} We measure AUROC (AUC) and accuracy (ACC) to benchmark all classification datasets (consistent with \citealt{yang2023medmnist}), and use Pearson's $r^2$ for all regression datasets. For all methods, we reserve the validation set of the datasets for hyperparameter tuning, and report all final accuracies on the test set.
For the 3D Medical MNIST dataset, we use the predetermined data splits from the benchmarks, allowing a direct comparison with prior and future works. For all other datasets without the standard splits, we use random training, validation, test splits of $60\%$/$20\%$/$20\%$.

