\section{Future Outlook and Conclusions.}
\label{sec:conclusion}
We proposed a novel PDE-based diffusion model based on the advection-diffusion equation. The model introduces a turbulent mixing term to the forward diffusion process, which, to our knowledge, has not been attempted before. 
In our experiments, we showed that adding the advective term besides the diffusion term improve the quality (FID) of generated images compared to the baseline approach (IHD)~\cite{Rissanen2022GenerativeMW}.
The external velocity field, which can transfer pixels' intensities in a spatially coherent way, offers a new way of introducing corruption into the forward process.  
In the future, the influence of different turbulence generators and the slope of turbulent kinetic energy can be further investigated. 
The interplay with a Gaussian noise corruption as proposed in \citet{hoogeboom2022blurring} also seems a natural direction of research.

