    % \item \textbf{Connecting the dots \cite{treutlein2024connecting}.} A base LLM is finetuned on a set of datapoints, each presenting partial information about a latent concept $z$ being learned, but many datapoints would have to be considered together to infer the value of $z$. For example, the latent concept might be an unknown function, and each datapoint is the value of this function on various inputs. See appendix \ref{connect-dots-tasks}. The model finetuned on this task is then able to use its knowledge of $z$ and apply it to out-of-distribution, downstream tasks, without any additional context. 
