\subsection{Remote and Local Cache Lines}
\label{subsection:remote_and_local}

A \emph{remote} cache line is one that was not previously inserted into the cache hierarchy by the accessing core. 
A \emph{local} cache line is one that was inserted into the cache hierarchy by the accessor core at a previous time. Remote cache lines are a security concern because their presence or absence can reveal to an attacker a secret that was used by a victim  on a different core. 




